# URL slugs

Public paths use a short Latin slug, not a transliteration of the full title.

## Shape

- Lowercase `a-z`, digits, hyphens. No underscores, no stop-words (`i`, `v`, `na`, `k`, `po`, `dlya`, `s`).
- One segment is the search keyword: 1–2 words, **at most 18 characters**.
- A nested sport URL is `/categories/{parent}/{child}`. The child does not repeat the parent word.
- Profiles: `/trainers/{slug}`, `/clubs/{slug}` — given name + family name, same length limit.
- Cities, blog, auth stay short and stable (`minsk`, `kak-vybrat-trenera`, `/auth/login`).
- Query filters are not indexable URLs.

## Examples

- `/categories/gimnastika/sportivnaya` — not `/categories/gimnastika-i-akrobatika/sportivnaya-gimnastika`
- `/categories/fitnes/personalnyj` — not `personalnyj-fitnes` under a parent that already says fitness
- `/categories/yoga`, `/categories/plavanie`, `/categories/zima/konki`

## When a slug changes

Keep the old segment in `src/lib/catalog/slug-policy.ts` (`LEGACY_CATALOG_SLUGS`) and redirect to the canonical path. Do not rename image files just because the slug changed.
